"title": "Hair, height, weight and appearance discrimination laws",
"what": "Places where a law, executive order or ordinance bans discrimination over hair texture or hairstyle (the CROWN Act and similar laws), height, weight or personal appearance. Almost all are in the United States: no worldwide compilation exists. Hair rows are taken from the table, executive-order and ordinance sections of the English Wikipedia article on hair discrimination in the US, which says \"As of December 2025, 27 out of 50 U.S. states and Puerto Rico\" have such laws. Height/weight/appearance rows come from the \"Law\" section of the Wikipedia article on height discrimination. Each row keeps the source that Wikipedia cites for it (cited_sources). Points are the Wikidata coordinates of the state, county or city (precision says which). Local ordinance rows have no date in the source.",
